581\u20131789, 402\u20131607\u20131708, 910\u2013913\u2013918, 557\u20131093\u20131422 (steps 04\u201308, 11\u201314, 23). Activity for these triads is concentrated in 19000\u201323500 (steps 22, 29), and 11 of the 12 triangle memberships are already closed by t=23500 (step_30); the final one (402\u20131607\u20131708) closes in (23500, 25400] (step_31). So the wave runs from ~19,400 and its last closing interaction lands at \u227225,400.\n\n**Part 2 \u2014 Temporal route 882 \u2192 1931.** 882 is active only around 25,472\u201325,571 and once near 27,300 (steps 15, 21). Its first contact is 882\u219263 at ~25,5xx (steps 17, 27). 63 reaches 816 (step_09), and 816\u2192291\u21921931 completes the path (step_10). The relay nodes {816, 291, 1931} fire at ~25,4xx, ~25,7\u201326,0xx and ~26,0\u201326,3xx (step_28), with 291\u21921931 confirmed inside [25700, 26300] (step_32). Every consecutive gap is a few hundred units \u2014 under the 600 limit \u2014 and the chain terminates by ~26,300 then goes silent (step_28), so it is a genuine ordered cascade, not diffuse background traffic.\n\n**Coupling.** Route onset \u224825,500 versus wave completion \u227225,400 \u2192 lag well under the 4,000-unit admissibility limit. The two phenomena are contiguous, not coincidentally co-located in a busy window: the group's triads and the 882-cascade occupy disjoint node sets (steps 04\u201314 vs 09\u201310), and the global window is sparse (repeat_ratio 0.0033, 3351 events over 1742 nodes, step_01), so neither part is explained by volume or hub popularity.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_bcf40ee2\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"compound\",\n  \"entities\": [40, 79, 122, 149, 239, 303, 315, 402, 550, 557, 664, 910, 882, 63, 816, 291, 1931],\n  \"window\": [18400, 36193],\n  \"confidence\": 0.68,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_30\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_31\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_29\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_32\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The 12 seed nodes form eight disjoint triads whose closing edges all land between ~19,400 and ~25,400, the last being 402-1607-1708 (11/12 closed by 23,500, 12/12 by 25,400). Immediately after, 882 emits its first event (882->63 at ~25,5xx) and a time-respecting chain 882->63->816->291->1931 completes by ~26,300 with every inter-step gap far below 600 units. The route begins within ~100-2,000 units of the wave's completion, comfortably inside the 4,000-unit admissible period, so the compound mechanism holds. Confidence is tempered because exact event timestamps for the closing edges were bracketed rather than read directly.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 103062, "total_output_tokens": 21421, "total_tokens": 124483, "total_latency_ms": 285477, "llm_calls": 13, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}